      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This canny is outdated. I learned later that the extra amount is an exact 20% to offset the transaction fees. The numbers are set such that an exact USD amount payed in by a buyer ($10) becomes an exact 50% paid out to the seller ($5). And CE sellers are encouraged to stick to prices that align with credit pack values.\n\nNow of course this doesn’t excuse the pricing of vrchat’s own items, but that’s a discussion for another canny.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-24T12:29:43.955Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This isn’t a scammy pay to win mobile game, there’s no reason to obfuscate the credit values by making the packs odd values. $5 should get you 500 credits, $20 should get you 2000, etc. We don’t need these things listed with $0.99 and “bonus” credits. Creators don’t want that, buyers don’t want that.\n\nStandardizing he values makes it easier for creators to price appropriately. And it makes buyers feel less like they’re being scammed.",
